Falsifies `filesystem_contract::dir::Rights::attenuate_never_widens`.

The defect: `attenuate` computes `self.0 | requested` instead of `self.0 & requested`.
One character, and it is the character the whole of the monotonicity property
rests on: the crate's own comment says "the whole of the monotonicity property
is this one `&`".

Expected to fail: `assert!(!child.allows(needed) || parent.allows(needed))`, whenever
`requested` holds a right the parent does not, which is exactly the escape a directory
capability must not permit.

**It also turns `a_grandchild_is_bounded_by_the_root` red**, and that is worth knowing
rather than hiding: the depth-2 harness has no falsification that the depth-1 harness
does not also catch, because `attenuate` is a single `&` and the only claim the second
harness adds is that AND is associative.

diff --git a/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs b/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs
--- a/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs
+++ b/crates/filesystem_contract/src/dir.rs
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@
     /// silently given less than it asked for, but that refusal is about telling the truth and
     /// this line is about the property.
     pub const fn attenuate(self, requested: u64) -> Self {
-        Rights(self.0 & requested)
+        Rights(self.0 | requested)
     }
 
     /// Whether this set carries **every** right in `needed`. Written as "all of", not "any of",
